# Stub for the relative import in /vendor/etc/init/hw/init.project.rc.
#
# init.project.rc line 3 reads:
#
#     import init.mt6765.usb.rc
#
# init resolves a relative import against its working directory, which is
# the filesystem root, so this looks for /init.mt6765.usb.rc. The real
# file lives at /vendor/etc/init/hw/init.mt6765.usb.rc and is already
# imported there by init.mt6765.rc line 4 using the correct absolute path,
# so nothing is lost here -- the stub exists only to stop init logging a
# parse error ("cannot open /init.mt6765.usb.rc") for the redundant line.
#
# If a future re-extraction ever ships a real /init.mt6765.usb.rc in the
# ramdisk, delete this file: the ramdisk copy would win.